{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg8qqsDmLw7L3yRzq2Tbs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] A player whose setup fails keeps its server hold and its armed subscriptions, because `closePlayer` never runs\n\nI fixed the finding. The full `npm test` run passes (4480/4480) and lint is clean.\n\n**What was wrong:** The review was right. `location-history` only calls a page's `destroy` once its `setup` has succeeded. When the file check inside `updatePlayer` failed, the server request and the engine subscriptions that `openPlayer` had already made were never released. One related problem: when a torrent has nothing playable, `playFile` ends up with index -1, and that crashed with a `TypeError` inside `isPlayable` before even reaching the `UnplayableFileError` path.\n\n**Fix:** `openPlayer` (`src/renderer/controllers/playback-controller.js:250`) now checks the file before it starts the server. If the file is missing or can't be played, it clears `mostRecentFileIndex` and calls back with `UnplayableFileError`. Nothing has been acquired at that point, so there is nothing to release, and `state.playing` stays as it was. I chose this over releasing things on the error path because it is the simpler of the two options the review offered. `updatePlayer` still does its own check, which next and previous rely on.\n\n**Tests:** I added three cases to `test/unit/playback-controller-subscriptions.js`: an unplayable file on a downloading torrent, the same on a paused torrent, and index -1. Each checks that no `wt-start-server` is sent and no subscription is left open. All three failed before the fix and pass after it. I also ran the file together with the other controller tests in both orders, because of the known collision between files that compile the same controller.\n\nThere are two commits. The second adds a note to `src/renderer/controllers/AGENTS.md` that a failed page `setup` is never destroyed. My notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":677,"cache_read_input_tokens":76992,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":677},"output_tokens":621,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"52417f48-72df-4c88-8824-cc460bf7ab25","uuid":"ea64c293-2775-4cb0-be4a-3cc25b91b847","timestamp":"2026-10-18T01:34:43.484Z","request_id":"req_011Cg8qqrxPJx6NC6MrhMaVT"}
